---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import profile from '../assets/profile.png';
import { AI_COURSE_URL, url } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="About" description="Lukas Lechner: AI engineering course creator, software developer with 15+ years of experience, blogger and speaker from Vienna.">
  <div class="container narrow page">
    <Image class="avatar" src={profile} alt="Portrait of Lukas Lechner" width={160} height={160} />
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Lukas Lechner</h1>

    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>AI Engineering</strong>: teaching developers to build production-ready LLM applications</li>
      <li><strong>15+ years</strong> as a software developer, on Android and the backend</li>
      <li><strong>Course creator</strong>, blogger and speaker at international developer conferences</li>
      <li><strong>MSc in Medical Informatics</strong> from the Technical University of Vienna</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Today I help software developers become AI engineers: building real applications on top of
        LLMs, with a pragmatic, no-hype path from developer to job-ready AI engineer. My course
        <a href={AI_COURSE_URL}>AI Engineering Fundamentals</a> covers the OpenAI API, prompt
        engineering, structured outputs and real portfolio projects.
        (<a href={url('from-android-to-ai-engineering/')}>Here's the story of how I got here.</a>)
      </p>
      <h2>How I got here</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a passionate software developer with over 15 years of experience. After compulsory school,
        I studied Medical Informatics at the <a href="https://www.tuwien.ac.at/en/">Technical University of Vienna</a>.
        During my studies, I worked for several companies, building database (SQL, PL/SQL) and C#
        applications.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2014 I discovered a real interest in mobile development (Android, to be specific) and
        jumped into that field after finishing my master's degree. At
        <a href="http://www.tailored-apps.com/">Tailored Apps</a>, Austria's leading mobile app agency,
        I worked on some of the country's biggest apps, such as
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.diepresse">die Presse</a>,
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=at.geizhals.pv">Geizhals</a> and
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=at.willhaben">willhaben</a>. After that, at
        <a href="http://riag.digital/">RIAG Digital</a> / <a href="https://www.rewe-group.at/">REWE Group</a>,
        I helped build state-of-the-art eCommerce apps like the
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=at.billa.service">Billa app</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        From 2020 I worked as a freelance Android developer for clients like Vienna Insurance Group
        (Austria), Roche (Switzerland) and SAP (Germany). In early 2023 I moved to backend development
        with Spring Boot, and in 2026 I went all in on AI Engineering.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2020 I also created my first online course, <a href={url('course/')}>Mastering Kotlin Coroutines
        for Android Development</a>, which has since grown into a 15-hour course on Coroutines and Flow.
        Many Android developers still know me as the "Coroutines & Flow guy". I
        <a href={url('talks/')}>spoke</a> at international conferences like droidcon Vienna, droidcon EMEA
        and droidcon Americas.
      </p>
      <p>
        On my <a href={url('blog/')}>blog</a>, I write about the topics I'm currently working on, which
        these days means AI Engineering.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to work together? <a href="mailto:contact@lukaslechner.com">contact@lukaslechner.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }
  .avatar {
    width: 6rem;
    height: 6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    outline: 5px solid var(--accent-soft);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.6rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }
  .facts {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .facts li {
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .facts strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
